  "caption": "Quinn, 38, bought a skateboard, met the first ramp, and landed on straight arms. The next day the wrist was still tender — but it moved, so it was fine… right?\n\nFalls at the skate park often load the wrists, elbows, ankles and shoulders, and head injuries are the serious risk. A wrist that moves can still be broken.\n\nWhat can help: a helmet every time (they're not just for kids), wrist guards and pads at the park, learning to roll rather than brace on straight arms, building leg strength first if you're returning as an adult, and finishing rehab before the next session.\n\nGet checked after any head knock, a suspected fracture, or a wrist still tender after a couple of days.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
